{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A6Bampm5srDwm4JTNwdk1P","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"vitest testNamePattern full name separator suite test \" > \" space\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"vitest.dev\",\"url\":\"https://vitest.dev/config/testnamepattern\"},{\"title\":\"docs.w3cub.com\",\"url\":\"https://docs.w3cub.com/vitest/config/testnamepattern\"},{\"title\":\"main.vitest.dev\",\"url\":\"https://main.vitest.dev/config/testnamepattern\"},{\"title\":\"Test Filtering\",\"url\":\"https://vitest.dev/guide/filtering\"},{\"title\":\"docs.w3cub.com\",\"url\":\"https://docs.w3cub.com/vitest/guide/filtering\"},{\"title\":\"main.vitest.dev\",\"url\":\"https://main.vitest.dev/guide/filtering\"},{\"title\":\"This documentation covers Vitest v2 (old version). For the latest version, see\",\"url\":\"https://v2.vitest.dev/guide/filtering\"},{\"title\":\"next.tangled.org\",\"url\":\"https://next.tangled.org/vitest.dev/vitest/blob/v3/docs/guide/filtering.md\"},{\"title\":\"next.tangled.org\",\"url\":\"https://next.tangled.org/vitest.dev/vitest/blob/v2/docs/guide/filtering.md\"},{\"title\":\"test suite\",\"url\":\"https://v3.vitest.dev/advanced/api/test-suite\"}]\n\nThe current Vitest docs say `testNamePattern` matches against a test's full name, which is the enclosing suite names and the test name joined with ` > `, the same string the reporter shows. So `-t 'math > adds'` and `-t adds` both match a test named `adds` inside `describe('math')`. The pattern is matched against the test's full name, and the docs give that `math > adds` example.\n\nThere's a version difference to note. The docs warn that before Vitest 5, the segments were joined with a single space (math adds) to mirror Jest. So on pre-5 releases, the separator is a space, not ` > `.\n\nThe docs also say the flag accepts a string or RegExp. The CLI flag is `-t` or `--testNamePattern`, and this can be helpful when you want to filter by the name defined 