{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvKG3pzbYKrY6R5N1626","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It depends on the Vitest version. According to the current Vitest docs, `testNamePattern` (`-t` / `--testNamePattern`) is matched against the test's full name. That full name is the enclosing `describe` names plus the test name, joined with **` > `**, which is the same string the reporter prints. So a test `adds` inside `describe('math')` has the full name `math > adds`, and both `-t 'math > adds'` and `-t adds` match it.\n\nThe docs also say that before Vitest 5 the parts were joined with a **single space** (`math adds`) to match Jest. On older versions, write patterns with spaces instead. The option takes a string or a RegExp. I got this from the docs through search results and didn't open the pages myself, so check the docs for your version if the exact separator matters.\n\nSources:\n- [vitest.dev – testNamePattern config](https://vitest.dev/config/testnamepattern)\n- [vitest.dev – Test Filtering guide](https://vitest.dev/guide/filtering)\n- [main.vitest.dev – testNamePattern](https://main.vitest.dev/config/testnamepattern)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":908,"cache_read_input_tokens":22540,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":908},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc267bd9-6172-49eb-b8a7-9d3249e50bcf","uuid":"ee85b801-ce5e-43af-bdde-5aae09d7661e","timestamp":"2026-10-11T10:46:27.255Z","request_id":"req_011CfvKG3Yt8MEPbSCSvtQCf"}
